They don't have additional items when they revive; they can create
random items with their corpse when they die (as can most monsters,
revived or not), but those random items were never in the inventory,
and may not be eligible to have been.

(The death-drop is just one of the historical oddities of NetHack; I
don't think there's any real reason for it to exist these days, but
there you go.)

